=== RUN   TestPullRequestTargetValidation/pull_request_target_with_checkout_enabled_-_non-strict_-_should_warn
/tmp/gh-aw-test-runs/20260715-163420-637166/prt-validation-test560864544/prt-checkout-enabled-non-strict.md: warning: pull_request_target trigger with checkout enabled is extremely insecure.

This event runs with full write permissions and access to repository secrets,
but the workflow will check out code from a potentially untrusted PR contributor.
This is a well-known attack vector: a fork PR can inject malicious code that
executes with access to your repository's secrets ("pwn request" attack).

Suggested fix: Use one of these safe patterns:
1) Disable checkout entirely:
checkout: false

2) Check out only the trusted base repo/ref:
checkout:
  repository: ${{ github.repository }}
  ref: ${{ github.event.pull_request.base.sha }}

3) Check out only the trusted base repository and omit ref:
checkout:
  repository: ${{ github.repository }}

You can also use 'ref: ${{ github.event.pull_request.base.ref }}'.
See: https://securitylab.github.com/resources/github-actions-preventing-pwn-requests/

